#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:13
msgid "Creating an animation"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:14
msgid "LET'S GET STARTED!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:16
msgid "Now that you know the SpriteFrames editor's interface, let's create a new animation from the ground up."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:19
msgid "In this tour, you'll learn the workflow for setting up looping character animations that you can use in your own games."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:37
msgid "Creating a new scene"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:43
msgid "Let's create our own animated sprite from scratch!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:44
msgid "Create a new scene by going to the Scene menu and selecting [b]New Scene[/b]."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:48
msgid "Create a new scene."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:59
msgid "Adding an AnimatedSprite2D node"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:65
msgid "Now click the %s [b]Add Node[/b] button at the top left of the Scene dock to open the node creation dialog."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:66
msgid "When the [b]Create New Node[/b] dialog appears, search for [b]AnimatedSprite2D[/b] and double-click it to add it to your scene."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:70
msgid "Create an AnimatedSprite2D node."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:90
msgid "Creating a SpriteFrames resource"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:112
msgid "The [b]AnimatedSprite2D[/b] node needs a [b]SpriteFrames[/b] resource to hold all its animations and frames."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:113
msgid "In the [b]Inspector[/b], ensure the Animation category is expanded and locate the [b]Sprite Frames[/b] property, which is currently empty."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:114
msgid "Click the dropdown arrow next to the empty field and select %s [b]New SpriteFrames[/b] to create the resource."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:118
msgid "Create a SpriteFrames resource."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:142
msgid "Opening the SpriteFrames editor"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:149
msgid "Click on the newly created [b]SpriteFrames[/b] resource in the Inspector. This will open the SpriteFrames editor at the bottom of the screen."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:153
msgid "Open the SpriteFrames editor."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:161
msgid "Renaming the default animation"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:167
msgid "You'll notice a \"default\" animation has already been created for you. Let's rename it to better match the animation we'll create."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:168
msgid "Click on [b]default[/b] in the animation list to rename it. Type [b]run[/b] and press Enter."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:169
msgid "It's important to give animations meaningful names because those are the names you'll use to play them in your GDScript code."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:173
msgid "Rename the default animation to 'run'."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:184
msgid "Adding frames to an animation"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:193
msgid "There are multiple ways to add frames to an animation. The easiest method is to drag and drop images from the FileSystem dock."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:194
msgid "Notice the folder [b]res://assets/lucy/run[/b] in the [b]FileSystem[/b] dock. That's where the sprites for Lucy's run animation are stored."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:200
msgid "Selecting multiple frames"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:205
msgid "Let's add frames to the run animation. To add multiple frames at once:"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:207
msgid "[b]Left click[/b] on the first image file, [b]000.png[/b]"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:208
msgid "Hold [b]Shift[/b] and [b]left click[/b] on the last file, [b]005.png[/b]"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:211
msgid "This selects all frames in between."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:215
msgid "Select all 6 run animation frames."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:237
msgid "Drag and drop frames"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:244
msgid "With the frames selected, drag and drop them into the [b]Frames View[/b] in the right side of the SpriteFrames editor."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:245
msgid "All the selected frames will be added to your [b]run[/b] animation in sequence."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:249
msgid "Add the 6 run frames to the animation."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:270
msgid "Looping animations"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:276
msgid "By default, animations are set to loop, meaning they'll play continuously rather than stopping after one cycle."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:277
msgid "You can toggle animation looping by clicking the %s [b]Loop[/b] icon above the animation list. For a run animation, we want looping enabled (the icon should be highlighted blue)."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:284
msgid "Previewing your animation"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:291
msgid "Let's see how the animation looks!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:292
msgid "Click the %s [b]Play[/b] button to preview your animation."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:295
msgid "Play the animation."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:299
msgid "Adjusting animation speed"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:304
msgid "Our run animation currently is too slow because the default animation framerate is low."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:305
msgid "We can adjust this by changing its frame rate using the [b]FPS[/b] (Frames Per Second) field above the animation list."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:306
msgid "Change the FPS value from [b]5.0[/b] to [b]10.0[/b]."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:307
msgid "Think of this like a flipbook: higher FPS means flipping through the frames faster. It also makes the animation more fluid."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:311
msgid "Change the FPS value to 10.0."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:322
msgid "Previewing the adjusted animation"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:327
msgid "Great job! Because the animation is looping, you can immediately see how the speed change affects the animation."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:328
msgid "For a running animation, 10-12 FPS usually gives a good result for pixel art characters."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:335
msgid "Conclusion"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:336
msgid "CONTINUE"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:338
msgid "Congratulations! You've completed the basics of using the [b]AnimatedSprite2D[/b] node to create flipbook-style animations in Godot."
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:341
msgid "You've learned how to:"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:343
msgid "Create and rename animations"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:344
msgid "Change animation playback settings like speed and looping"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:345
msgid "Add frames by dragging image files into the editor"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:346
msgid "Preview your animations directly in the editor"
msgstr ""

#: tours/102_creating_animation/102_creating_animation.gd:350
msgid "In the next tour, we'll explore more tools to adjust the timing of individual frames, copy and paste frames, and create more complex animation patterns."
msgstr ""
